# Code owners — the review gate for paths where a wrong merge is expensive.
#
# Most of this repository merges on green CI with no approval required, so
# ordinary work moves at the speed of the test suite. The paths below are the
# exception: a mistake in them is costly, slow to notice, or hard to walk back
# once published, so each one stops for a deliberate human look.
#
# Note on mechanics: GitHub does not let anyone approve their own pull request.
# With a single owner, a PR touching these paths cannot be approved by its
# author — it stops, and merging it is a conscious override rather than a
# click. That is the intended behavior: the gate is a stop sign, not a queue.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supply chain — what gets built, published, and executed in CI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
